```go
func zero(s []int) { s[0] = 0 }
nums := []int{1, 2, 3}
zero(nums)   // nums is now [0 2 3]
```
The slice header was copied but the backing array was not, so the write is visible to the caller. Change `zero` to `append` instead and the caller may see nothing, because append can allocate a new array — the same argument behaves differently depending on whether you write or grow.

